The attached image shows confocal microscopy images of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) demonstrating the uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles and ovalbumin (OVA). The top row illustrates efficient phagocytosis of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) by BMDCs. The middle row indicates minimal uptake of soluble FITC-labeled OVA (green). The bottom row clearly shows significantly enhanced uptake and co-localization of both Nano-11 and OVA when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 (yellow/orange in merged image), highlighting Nano-11's role in improving antigen delivery to dendritic cells, a critical step for vaccine adjuvancy as discussed in the PDF.